# The companion to 369: PARTIAL overlap is not that error and never becomes
# one. Two boxes that clip each other are ugly and both readable, which is the
# `novlp` axis's business in tools/layout-lint.js — "ugly is not an error;
# wrong is", and the line between them is whether any ink of the covered node
# survives. Both nodes below are pinned to overlap by 40x20 px, and the figure
# renders with no geometry diagnostic at all.
figdown 0.1 block
title "Two boxes that clip each other are drawn"
node a "A"
node b "B"
pin a at=(0,0) width=120 height=60
pin b at=(80,40) width=120 height=60
edge a -> b
